    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The counts palatine of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rhine">Rhine</a> ruled scattered Rhineland lands from Heidelberg and were imperial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#prince-elector">electors</a> from 1356.</li><li>It was the leading Reformed Protestant state of the Empire and the home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#heidelberg-catechism">Heidelberg Catechism</a> of 1563.</li><li>Frederick V's acceptance of the Bohemian crown in 1619 began its ruin; in 1803 its last lands were divided among Baden and others.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Much of Heidelberg's great library, the Bibliotheca Palatina, was sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rome">Rome</a> in 1623 as a gift to the pope after the city fell, and it remains in the Vatican Library.</p></aside>
    </section>

